Z||000000||dravenhawk||02-06-2000||11:46 PM||||if i plan on replacing springs and shocks and other handling components as well as an engine swap, does it matter what year and model to purchase?<P>dravenhawk||||reg||5
Z||000001||dravenhawk||02-07-2000||12:16 AM||||is it true that putting a v6 in an 84 is much harder and different than in 85-88's?<P>dravenhawk||||reg||1
Z||000003||88GT||02-07-2000||03:10 AM||||As years go I would go with an 88 as they have the newer suspension.  I have seen them with reasonable prices (and some not so reasonable).  Get the model you want.  This is going to be more for body style and interior. If you are going to upgrade suspension, engine and drivetrain anyway; then those parts don't matter. <p>[This message has been edited by 88GT (edited 02-07-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||88GT||02-07-2000||03:11 AM||||As years go I would go with an 88 as they have the newer suspension.  I have seen them with reasonable prices (and some not so reasonable).  Get the model you want.  This is going to be more for body style and interior. If you are going to upgrade suspension, engine and drivetrain anyway; then those parts don't matter. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||sdm1964||02-07-2000||06:34 AM||||The 88 suspension will not fit the 84-87 without major modification. I also beleive the v-6 is no harder to put in an 84 than any other year, have to change dog bone, motor mounts, etc. I think i am correct on this, just what i learned from this forum||||reg||14
Z||000006||DRH||02-07-2000||01:43 PM||||I believe the wiring might be a little harder putting a V6 in an 84. If I'm not mistaken the main wiring harness connector plugs into the firewall on an 84 and near the battery on other years.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||02-07-2000||07:24 PM||||Since V6 was not an option in 84 there may not be any holes in the 84 cradle for it. You would need the cradle out of a V6 Fiero in that case.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Standard||02-08-2000||02:14 AM||||I think you do have to use a v6 cradle for an 84, not sure tho.  I do know that the main wiring harness connector plugs are in the firewall.  If you're going to swap a v6 into a 4cyl car, i'd look for an 85.  Stay away from 84's if you want performance.||||reg||1
